<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alatri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aletrium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alatri, ancient Aletrium, is a hill town of the Hernici in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazio">Lazio</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, famous for its acropolis enclosed by massive polygonal walls of the pre-Roman period. Loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> during the Hernican revolt of 306 BCE, it remained an allied city with its own laws before receiving Roman citizenship after the Social War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alatri.jpg" alt="Alatri" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Fabiosbaraglia at Italian Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Paolo_Alatri_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
